# GIT ignore file:

*
*.*

# Apple specific files:

.DS_Store

# Explicit allow Markdown Files
#
# THIS LINE HAS TO STAY BELOW THE EXCLUSIONS. In a .gitignore the LAST matching
# rule wins, so an exception written above `*` and `*.*` is silently undone by
# them -- which is what happened here until 2026-09-13: `git add SECURITY.md`
# reported "The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files"
# and `git commit` then found nothing to commit. The sibling repository
# edutap-collective/.github already had the same three rules in the working
# order; this file now matches it.
!*.md
